{
  "title": "Normals",
  "description": "Where a material takes its surface normals from. Every entry is also exported under its own name - normalMap, normalsFromAlpha. The two spellings do the same thing, and only the named one lets a bundler drop what you did not use: reaching one property of this object keeps the whole object, and with it the Sobel derivation and the canvas readback behind `fromAlpha`. Reach for the named form when the bundle matters, and for this one when discoverability does.",
